  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    if not grid:\n        return []\n    \n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    \n    # Create output as a deep copy of input\n    output = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    \n    # Track visited cells\n    visited = [[False] * cols for _ in range(rows)]\n    \n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[r][c] != 0 and not visited[r][c]:\n                # Find the connected component using DFS\n                color = grid[r][c]\n                stack = [(r, c)]\n                visited[r][c] = True\n                cells = []\n                \n                while stack:\n                    cr, cc = stack.pop()\n                    cells.append((cr, cc))\n                    # Check 4 neighbors: up, down, left, right\n                    for dr, dc in [(-1, 0), (1, 0), (0, -1), (0, 1)]:\n                        nr, nc = cr + dr, cc + dc\n                        if 0 <= nr < rows and 0 <= nc < cols and not visited[nr][nc] and grid[nr][nc] == color:\n                            visited[nr][nc] = True\n                            stack.append((nr, nc))\n                \n                # Calculate bounding box of the component\n                min_r = min(cell[0] for cell in cells)\n                max_r = max(cell[0] for cell in cells)\n                min_c = min(cell[1] for cell in cells)\n                max_c = max(cell[1] for cell in cells)\n                \n                # Check if the component forms a solid rectangle\n                height = max_r - min_r + 1\n                width = max_c - min_c + 1\n                \n                # If it's a solid rectangle, clear its interior\n                if len(cells) == height * width:\n                    for i in range(min_r + 1, max_r):\n                        for j in range(min_c + 1, max_c):\n                            output[i][j] = 0\n    \n    return output\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    if not grid:\n        return []\n    \n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    \n    # Create output as a deep copy of input\n    output = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    \n    # Track visited cells\n    visited = [[False] * cols for _ in range(rows)]\n    \n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[r][c] != 0 and not visited[r][c]:\n                # Find the connected component using DFS\n                color = grid[r][c]\n                stack = [(r, c)]\n                visited[r][c] = True\n                cells = []\n                \n                while stack:\n                    cr, cc = stack.pop()\n                    cells.append((cr, cc))\n                    # Check 4 neighbors: up, down, left, right\n                    for dr, dc in [(-1, 0), (1, 0), (0, -1), (0, 1)]:\n                        nr, nc = cr + dr, cc + dc\n                        if 0 <= nr < rows and 0 <= nc < cols and not visited[nr][nc] and grid[nr][nc] == color:\n                            visited[nr][nc] = True\n                            stack.append((nr, nc))\n                \n                # Calculate bounding box of the component\n                min_r = min(cell[0] for cell in cells)\n                max_r = max(cell[0] for cell in cells)\n                min_c = min(cell[1] for cell in cells)\n                max_c = max(cell[1] for cell in cells)\n                \n                # Check if the component forms a solid rectangle\n                height = max_r - min_r + 1\n                width = max_c - min_c + 1\n                \n                # If it's a solid rectangle, clear its interior\n                if len(cells) == height * width:\n                    for i in range(min_r + 1, max_r):\n                        for j in range(min_c + 1, max_c):\n                            output[i][j] = 0\n    \n    return output",
